      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1842 surveyor Robert Hoddle named the suburb after Lord Horatio Nelson's admiral Cuthbert Collingwood, or a hotel bearing his name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collingwood%2C_Victoria",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The suburb boomed during the Gold Rush, attracting immigrants and spawning factories for shoe, wool, and textile manufacturing by the late 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        6,
        19,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://tomelbourne.com/history-of-collingwood/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Many nineteenth‑century factories and shops still stand, and modern apartments now occupy former warehouses like those of Foy & Gibson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
